From f5400a7174eaf3d19d09fe59092d39a9b6eb53ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Brunner <michael.brunner@sm0x.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:12:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] elan: fix decoding of the calibration mean

The device reports the calibration mean as a big-endian 16 bit value, but
the driver combines the two bytes with a factor of 0xff instead of 0x100:

    calib_mean = last_read[0] * 0xff + last_read[1];

That mapping is not injective.  Of the 65536 possible byte pairs only
65281 distinct values can be produced, and 255 pairs collide - for
example (11, 255) and (12, 0) both decode to 3060.  A byte decoding that
maps distinct inputs onto the same value cannot be correct regardless of
what the device actually reports.

In practice the resulting value is too small by the high byte, which for
the observed range around 2900 is an error of about 11 counts.  That
stays well below ELAN_CALIBRATION_MAX_DELTA (500), so the recalibration
decision is unaffected in the common case.  It can still shift borderline
cases, and the value is printed in the debug log where it invites
comparison with the background mean computed from the actual frame.

Found while re-implementing the ELAN protocol against an 04f3:0c63 in
order to capture raw frames for analysis.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libfprint/drivers/elan.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
index f9cc52f..e51f1c8 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
@@ -651,7 +651,7 @@ elan_need_calibration (FpiDeviceElan *elandev)
   G_DEBUG_HERE ();
 
   unsigned short calib_mean =
-    elandev->last_read[0] * 0xff + elandev->last_read[1];
+    (elandev->last_read[0] << 8) | elandev->last_read[1];
   unsigned int bg_mean = 0, delta;
   unsigned int frame_size = elandev->frame_width * elandev->frame_height;
 
